.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
node_modules/
playwright-report/
test-results/
*.log

# Secrets -- GROQ_API_KEY / etc. Never commit these; orca/agentic.py reads
# them from the environment only, and only from the backend process (a
# key must never be reachable from web/*.js -- that's shipped to the
# browser as-is, no build step, no bundler, fully visible via view-source).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Mobile build artifacts. docs/MOBILE_APP.md §7 is explicit that these
# must be ignored BEFORE the first mobile commit, not after -- Gradle
# caches and build outputs are large, binary, and regenerated on every
# build. The APK itself is a build output too: it is produced by
# `gradle assembleRelease`, not committed.
mobile/android/build/
mobile/android/app/build/
mobile/android/.gradle/
mobile/android/local.properties
mobile/android/**/*.iml
*.apk
*.aab

# Fleet-reported readings (orca/observations.py). Runtime-collected data,
# not source. Quarantined from data/cache/ by design; see
# docs/MOBILE_APP.md §5. A real deployment needs a durable store and a
# named person running QC -- that is open question 4 in that document, and
# gitignoring this is NOT an answer to it.
data/observations/
